WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:04.400
Hi, I'm Vivek Kinra from the IBM&nbsp;
Cloud Hyper Protect Services team.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:09.680
Today, we're going to talk about Confidential&nbsp;
Computing as provided by Hyper Protect.  

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:15.840
So, why Confidential Computing? 
Data security and protection are by far

00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:20.880
the biggest inhibitors for organizations&nbsp;
seeking to move sensitive applications&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:26.640
and data to the public cloud. 
In fact, 95% of our customers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:33.440
in regulated industry cited security, privacy,&nbsp;
regulatory concerns and cloud provider having a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:40.000
backdoor access to organizations sensitive data as&nbsp;
their main inhibitors for using a public cloud. 

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:45.520
To address these concerns, we are talking&nbsp;
about three pillars of data security&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:52.480
when considering end-to-end data protection.  
Data at rest and data in flight are the two

00:00:52.480 --> 00:00:58.240
pillars that historically have received the&nbsp;
most attention and addresses many concerns.

00:00:59.120 --> 00:01:05.280
However, when regulated industries clients&nbsp;
bring their sensitive workloads to the IBM Cloud&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:10.160
Hyper Protect Services, they want&nbsp;
to process their sensitive data with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.160 --> 00:01:15.920
highest level of data protection without&nbsp;
compromising the performance and latency.

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:21.280
So, to complete the data protection&nbsp;
lifecycle, client wants to protect

00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:27.360
their data when it in use, or in memory.
This is the focus of confidential computing.

00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:35.280
The IBM Cloud Hyper Protect Services, including&nbsp;
Crypto Services, Virtual Servers and DBaaS offer

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:41.040
protection for all 3 pillars thereby providing&nbsp;
an end-to-end confidential computing environment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:43.840
in the IBM Cloud.
So, how does IBM

00:01:43.840 --> 00:01:49.600
provide this level of security?
Well, the Hyper Protect Services leverage

00:01:49.600 --> 00:01:53.840
many years of IBM's security and
privacy experience to the Cloud. 

00:01:54.720 --> 00:02:00.560
To do this, we deploy our services on 
special LinuxONE hardware that utilizes

00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:06.560
what's known as a Secure Service Container.
This is a protective boundary around the base

00:02:06.560 --> 00:02:12.800
operating system, management backend&nbsp;
and application interface to ensure no

00:02:12.800 --> 00:02:17.760
access by the unauthorized figures like system&nbsp;
administrators or the cloud providers.  
 &nbsp;

00:02:18.640 --> 00:02:25.120
Secure Service Container ensures: 
Data Integrity and self-attestation - There&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.120 --> 00:02:30.720
is  tamper protection and verification through&nbsp;
signatures that the packaged software image is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:35.840
deployed from a trusted source and not&nbsp;
been modified since leaving the vendor.&nbsp;

00:02:36.560 --> 00:02:41.680
In case any tamper is detected,&nbsp;
Secure Service Container will not boot that image.  
 &nbsp;

00:02:42.320 --> 00:02:46.960
There are several examples of client&nbsp;
segments from financial institutes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.960 --> 00:02:52.400
automotive manufacturers to start-ups who are&nbsp;
currently using the Hyper Protect Services&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:58.000
to achieve confidential computing. 
Today, we're going to explore one particular

00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:04.720
use case, the Digital Assets Platform.
With this use case, clients are tokenizing

00:03:04.720 --> 00:03:08.320
and trading assets, similarly to&nbsp;
how the stock market works.

00:03:08.960 --> 00:03:14.880
However, the assets aren't shares of a company,&nbsp;
they can range from coins to commodities.

00:03:15.600 --> 00:03:19.520
With our digital assets platform,&nbsp;
you have the asset itself,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.520 --> 00:03:21.840
that is run by a combination of 3 things.&nbsp;

00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:26.480
A base technology, Blockchain,&nbsp;
that provides the ledger.

00:03:27.120 --> 00:03:31.840
The Wallets, to protect keys.
And Exchanges, or the digital marketplace. 

00:03:32.640 --> 00:03:38.320
To provide a confidential computing environment&nbsp;
for the Digital Assets Platform, first,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.320 --> 00:03:43.920
we utilize protected runtimes with Hyper Protect&nbsp;
Virtual Servers to actually run the application.&nbsp;

00:03:44.560 --> 00:03:50.720
These run within a Secure Service Container that&nbsp;
automatically encrypts data and provides memory&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.720 --> 00:03:55.760
protection to ensure that no unauthorized&nbsp;
person gets access to secure data. 

00:03:56.400 --> 00:04:02.400
Next, we work with the Hyper Protect Crypto&nbsp;
Services to utilize the Hardware Security Module,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.400 --> 00:04:09.920
or HSM, and Key Management Service.
With this technology, built on FIPS 140-2 Level 4&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.920 --> 00:04:14.800
certified hardware, clients can&nbsp;
lock down their storage, backups,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.800 --> 00:04:20.320
Secure Service Container, and applications.
Finally, we work with other IBM Cloud offerings

00:04:20.320 --> 00:04:26.080
to provide backup and storage, also integrated&nbsp;
with Crypto Services, and holistically&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.080 --> 00:04:30.400
locking down the entire environment.
In this way, we protect from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.400 --> 00:04:36.400
malicious actors in several ways.
They cannot SSH into the boundary, the wallets and

00:04:36.400 --> 00:04:42.560
ledgers are stored in Cold Storage, or offline,&nbsp;
with encrypted communications, and the Secure&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.560 --> 00:04:48.080
Service Container is tamper-proof and will prevent&nbsp;
unauthorized access through these back doors.

00:04:49.520 --> 00:04:53.680
So, with that example in mind, there&nbsp;
are 2 reasons to choose Hyper Protect&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.680 --> 00:04:58.640
for Confidential Computing:
First, clients maintain complete authority&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.640 --> 00:05:04.240
over their workloads. They have exclusive&nbsp;
control of who sees the data, what happens

00:05:04.240 --> 00:05:10.320
to that data and how that data is processed.
Second, client data and applications are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:10.320 --> 00:05:16.000
protected from both insider and outsider&nbsp;
threats. There is technical assurance,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:20.640
not just operational assurance.
We go beyond the confidential computing

00:05:20.640 --> 00:05:28.560
environment to protect data at all stages, in&nbsp;
flight, at-rest, and in-use, plus the complete&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.560 --> 00:05:34.160
authority that only comes with IBM Cloud.
With that, thank you for listening to this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:34.160 --> 00:05:38.640
brief overview of IBM Cloud Hyper&nbsp;
Protect Services and their role&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:38.640 --> 00:05:50.960
in the confidential computing environment.
